#### Dietary Sources

Roughage is primarily `found in plant`-based foods:

* **Whole Grains &amp; Seeds:** Entire seeds, pulses, and peas.
* **Produce:** Potatoes, vegetables, and unpeeled fruits.
* **Other Sources:** Dried fruits, cumin, and coriander.
:::
:::
</md></sn><sn><md>### Importance and Benefits of Roughage

+++ view
![img](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-em0n/QDoc/main/BCS/General%20Science/B.Z.Food%20and%20Nutrition/assets/benefits_of_fibre.png)
+++

1. **Aids Digestion:** `Absorbs water` and `adds bulk to stool` to facilitate smooth bowel movements.
2. **Waste Elimination:** Helps `clear undigested food` materials from the body.
3. **Weight &amp; Fat Management:** Helps `reduce body fat` and curbs frequent `hunger cravings`.
4. **Disease Prevention:** Associated with a `reduced risk of gallbladder diseases`, intestinal and colon cancers, hemorrhoids (piles), appendicitis, heart disease, and obesity.

</md></sn><sn><md>#### Recommended Daily Intake

It is recommended to consume `20–30 grams of fiber daily`, best sourced through a ++diet++ rich in `fruits and vegetables`.</md></sn>